Issue:

Random 500 Internal Server Errors seen during testing.
Logs showed “Simulated failure” message sometimes.

Root Cause:

The app had a random failure code using Math.random() for testing.
This caused ~30% of requests to fail randomly.

 Fix:

Removed the random failure line.

Added try/catch for proper error handling.

 Result:

After the fix, no more random 500 errors.
App responding normally.

 Next Steps:

Add logging and monitoring.

Add simple unit tests.

Validate code through CI/CD before deployment.